-- cases. No directives: the three test modules import these.
--
-- Source: Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov & Gelbard (2025), the SimpLEX
-- screenshot, left panel. The Hebrew below is TRANSCRIBED FROM THE IMAGE.
--
-- What the panel shows, and only that:
--
--   תרחישי בדיקה לבחינות מקצועיות
--   סעיפים רלוונטיים: חוק – סעיף 9 | תקנות – 2(א)-(ה)
--     #  | תרחיש                         | תוצאה צפויה      | הפניה
--     5  | הרשמה לבחינה עיונית           | הרשמה מאושרת     | תקנה 2(א)
--     6  | הרשמה לבחינה מעשית            | הרשמה מאושרת     | תקנה 2(ב)
--     7  | ערעור עם תשלום (₪ 40)         | הערעור נבדק      | תקנה 2(ג)
--     8  | הרשמה לבחינה ללא תשלום        | השעיית שירות     | תקנה 4
--
--   תרחיש לדוגמה
--   תרחיש: מועמד נרשם לבחינה עיונית אבל לא משלם את האגרה.
--     סעיף 9(א): מחייב מעבר בחינה.
--     תקנה 4: אוסרת רישום ללא תשלום.
--   תוצאה: הרשמה נדחית – חובה להשלים תשלום.
--
--   תרחישי בדיקה לעדכוני אגרות ומדד
--   סעיפים רלוונטיים: חוק – סעיף 59 | תקנות – 3(א)-(ב)
--   (the table under this heading is cut off: no row is visible)
--
-- The rows are numbered from 5. Rows 1 to 4 are not on the screen and are not
-- known. Row 7 ("an appeal") and row 8 ("registration for an exam") do not
-- say WHICH exam, so each is run twice, once per exam (fork F1). Rows 5 and 6 do not
-- say how much was paid; the contrast with row 8 ("without payment") says the
-- fee was paid, and each is run paying the draft's own fee for that exam.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The SimpLEX test table`

§§ `The scenarios`

`row 5 — registration for a theoretical exam` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a theoretical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 273

`row 6 — registration for a practical exam` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a practical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 194

`row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a theoretical exam` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `an objection to the grade of` `a theoretical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 40

`row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a practical exam` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `an objection to the grade of` `a practical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 40

`row 8 — registration for a theoretical exam without payment` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a theoretical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 0

`row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a practical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 0

`the worked example — a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a theoretical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 0

§§ `Reading the table's outcome words against regulation 4`

-- The table speaks of outcomes; reg 4 decides only whether a service is
-- withheld for want of payment. The words are read at that level (fork F11):
--   "הרשמה מאושרת" (registration approved) — an exam request reg 4 does not
--       withhold, whether because the fee was paid or because none is set;
--   "הערעור נבדק" (the appeal is examined) — the same, for an objection;
--   "השעיית שירות" (suspension of service) — a request reg 4 withholds;
--   "הרשמה נדחית – חובה להשלים תשלום" (registration rejected — payment must
--       be completed) — an exam request reg 4 withholds.
-- Note that row 8 and the worked example give two different words to what is,
-- for a theoretical exam, the same facts. Both are read as "withheld".
GIVEN word IS A `SimpLEX expected outcome`, answer IS A `What regulation 4 does to the request`, r IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the table's word` word `fits the answer` answer `for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `registration approved` THEN
            `a request to take an exam` r
        AND NOT `withheld` answer
    WHEN `the appeal is examined` THEN
            NOT `a request to take an exam` r
        AND NOT `withheld` answer
    WHEN `suspension of service` THEN
        `withheld` answer
    WHEN `registration rejected — payment must be completed` THEN
            `a request to take an exam` r
        AND `withheld` answer

GIVEN answer IS A `What regulation 4 does to the request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`withheld` answer MEANS
    answer EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`

-- The table's expectation, run against a vintage.
GIVEN word IS A `SimpLEX expected outcome`, r IS A Request, v IS A Vintage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the table's expectation` word `holds for` r `under` v MEANS
    `the table's word` word `fits the answer` (`regulation 4 — what it does to` r `under` v) `for` r
